      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-148173",
      ":question/problem": "The joint probability mass function $f(x, y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y = 1$ | $Y = 2$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $X = 0$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X = 1$ | $0.3$ | $0.5$ |\n\nGiven that $E[X] = 0.8$ and $E[Y] = 1.6$, find the covariance matrix for $X$ and $Y$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
